# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# NOT-12: while a full-screen page is up, nothing reaches the program.
# not-log-modal.leg's claim for the screen M5-E4d (#305) added, and the
# same claim because it is the same situation: the party's own
# command-bar routine is live underneath, which is why the page may take
# the whole screen, so a key this seam left alone would pick a command or
# walk the party where nobody could see it (#230).
# A single leg for not-log-modal.leg's reason: the seam-off run has no
# page to swallow those keys, so the two runs end in different states.

about nothing reaches the program while a full-screen page is up
kind single
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt

# #301's cheat puts everything the store holds onto the log, so the listing
# has a row to open. A citation is a place in the story, and a leg that had
# to walk to one would be testing the walk.
cite-all
both code-wheel

# The code-wheel bypass is gated on the wheel itself (#115), pinned by
# digest because a document never enters this tree.
document 0db301aeac4d2ec1e63b409ca6d3c9d39c63381d6712ff2ce7edc0528c6586fd
seam journal
until 300000000
every 25

# A screen this seam draws is painted over successive arrivals, a few
# rows at a time, by the program's own drawing routines: about 230
# frames for a twenty-row page and about 130 for a ten-row listing,
# measured by hand (#305). A range starting sooner would measure the
# paint.
key A@7601
key Return@7651
key L@8951
key A@9201

# The listing, then the row the cursor is already on, then the barrage:
# search, cast, look, three the party walks by, and the letter the
# listing's own bottom row names, which is not a way out of a page.
key N@10600
key Return@11200
key S@11800
key C@12000
key L@12200
key Left@12400
key Right@12600
key Up@12800

# And then the way out, which `E` is: the page's own bar says `EXIT` and
# the letter of a word on a bar is how this game leaves every screen it has
# (M5-E4f #317). The `same` line below stops short of it.
key E@13100

# From the page settling to the last of the barrage, one frame.
same 11500-13075
